This is an original automation script. It installs Harbor and orchestrates the
following third-party open-source software, each under its own license (all credit
to their respective authors):

  Harbor                  Apache-2.0     https://github.com/goharbor/harbor
  Docker / Moby           Apache-2.0     https://github.com/moby/moby

The Harbor offline installer bundle that this script downloads and (re)distributes
contains multiple upstream container images, each under its own license, e.g.:

  registry / distribution Apache-2.0
  Trivy                   Apache-2.0     https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy
  Notary                  Apache-2.0
  nginx (proxy)           BSD-2-Clause   https://nginx.org/
  PostgreSQL              PostgreSQL License
  Redis                   VERSION-DEPENDENT — older releases BSD-3-Clause; newer
                          Redis may be RSALv2 / SSPL (source-available, NOT OSI-open).
                          VERIFY the Redis version shipped by your pinned Harbor
                          release before redistributing the bundle.

When redistributing the Harbor offline bundle, retain each image's copyright/
license notices and any bundled NOTICE files.

The air-gap bundle that `offline-prep` builds also holds OS packages: Docker CE, containerd,
curl and what they depend on, each under its own license. Some are copyleft, including
iptables (GPL-2.0-or-later), and GnuTLS, librtmp and libidn2 (LGPL). The bundle's LICENSES/
folder lists them and carries a written offer for their source. LICENSE_OFFER_CONTACT sets who
it names. When you redistribute a bundle, that offer is yours to honor.
